        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) Preferred Recall List – An employee laid off for lack of work shall be given two (2) pay periods notice, following notice to the Union, and shall be placed on a preferred recall list for the length of time that he or she retains his or her Company seniority, as provided in Article IX, paragraph (4)(d) or (e). During each period, he or she shall not accrue credits for vacation and sick leave but shall be credited with the Company and departmental seniority if such employee is recalled before the end of the period. If the employee has not been recalled at the end of such period, he or she shall be removed from the preferred recall list and his or her employment shall be terminated. If he or she is thereafter employed by the Company, such employee shall be considered a new employee and classified as a probationer.",
